    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="dce59cb9-51ef-593d-ab26-a9892fba6d42" activityNameId="11c1da1d-2db7-5255-bd72-90a31cb8594a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Softwood, standing, under bark, holzpur, in forest</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Softwood, standing, under bark, holzpur, in forest
The volume refers to the wood not including the bark. CO2 assimilation is based on 49.4% carbon in the dry wood including the bark (10%). Biomass energy equals the gross calorific value of softwood including the bark. Data on the land use and the dry density are specific for the Korporation Giswil, which delivers the wood to Walter Küng AG for the production of holzpur elements. Land use type changed to "forest, intensive" (original: "forest, intensive, normal") for differentiation of use intensity in the KBOB recommendation 2016 (project 563).;
UUID: 1db6c58f-440f-3e84-9537-8d6a565ed1d0
Includes CO2 absorption from air and the land use for trees to grow. Forest road area is not included in the land use.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at the Korporation Giswil in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1db6c58f-440f-3e84-9537-8d6a565ed1d0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
